{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790342208,"nonce":"9f139OQebJnyuDruUwdgtHe556E=","title":"Each lazily compiled function takes at least one fresh JIT code page","message":"cranelift-jit's SystemMemoryProvider (pinned wasmtime rev) calls finish_current and allocates a new region per finalize, and every lazy compile finalizes, so every compiled function costs at least a 16 KB page on the Mac.\n\nEvidence: a Lua program of 300 one-line global functions peaked at 76.9 MB RSS with 437 VM_ALLOCATE regions holding 6.9 MB; locals.lua zt holds 50 MB of JIT code.\n\nSavings: about 12 KB per compiled small function; several MB to tens of MB on the official files.\n\nFix: pack compiled functions into shared pages (cranelift-jit's ArenaMemoryProvider or our own provider with a per-finalize W^X switch). Package MEM-jit-code-arena.","files":null}]}